# Enterprise Concepts Learned

This sprint introduced several foundational enterprise administration concepts:

- Organizational Units provide logical separation and simplify Group Policy deployment.
- Security Groups enable scalable role-based access control rather than assigning permissions directly to users.
- Service Accounts allow enterprise applications to authenticate securely without using personal user accounts.
- Dedicated administrative accounts reduce operational risk and improve accountability.
- Snapshot management provides safe rollback points before major infrastructure changes.

